+## Subtopics
+
+### Recolorable Textures with Palette Color
+Extends textured Gaussians with a learnable palette color $c_{pal}$ to enable real-time color editing by shifting the view-independent color [S2]. Initialize $c_{pal}$ as the mean color of input multi-view images [S2]. Optimize $c_{pal}$ and recolorable textures using RGB reconstruction loss $L_c$ combined with L1 sparsity regularization on $c_{tex}$ [S2]. Enable real-time color editing by adjusting $c_{pal}$ during inference [S2]. The view-independent color is computed as $c_{ind} = c_{pal} + (c_{tex})_i(p_i)$, where $c_{pal}$ is shared across all Gaussians in a basic scene, and $(c_{tex})_i(p_i)$ is the sampled texture color [S2].
